SWEET performance counters (patch 0145, boot-arg sweetperf=1, default off; G-10 / research 51 step 3): READ-ONLY accounting in the Mali job path (no register access, no new hardware write; review docs/reviews/0145-perf-counters.md SAFE WITH CONDITIONS, F1 and the boot-arg hoist applied): per second `SWEET PERF: gpu_jobs N busy_ms M max_job_us X submit_wait_ms W cpu_busy_pct P` = jobs finished, GPU busy time (submit -> completion seen), longest job, time submitters blocked behind the previous job (includes the ready check and lock contention, F2), and the CPU busy share from host_statistics64(HOST_CPU_LOAD_INFO).
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_mali.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_mali.c
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@
 #include <kern/thread.h>
